/**
   * Session-scoped memory for the Student Achievement list filters.
   *
   * The Status flyout and the Prior course flyout are client-side controls: they narrow a
   * cohort the browser already holds and never tell the server anything. Left alone they
   * also forget everything on every page
   * load, so a lecturer who opened a student's profile in a new tab, or came back to the
   * dashboard from an email, arrived at the whole class again and re-picked the same
   * filters (user request 2026-08-10).
   *
   * sessionStorage rather than a user preference or the server session: the ask was for
   * the tab's lifetime, and this is the only store that needs no round trip — these
   * controls fire on every tick, and a filter that lagged a request behind the list would
   * be worse than one that forgets. The cost is that a second tab starts clean and
   * closing the browser clears it, which is what "session only" means.
   *
   * Deliberately NOT remembered: the triage tab, the name search and the page. A search
   * is a hunt for one student and is over when you have found them, and a remembered page
   * number describes a list that may no longer have that many pages.
   *
   * @module     local_ace/achievement_filter_state
   * @copyright  2026 University of Canterbury
   * @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
   */
